    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "MRS. DOUGLAS MAC ARTHUR\nA.P.O. 500 c/ o POSTMASTER\nSAN FRANCISCO. CAL.\nJuly 18, 1949\nDear Debby:\nHow very sweet you were to send me the\nlovely little white bag by tarold and\nthank you far more than I can say.\nIt is some-\nthing I need and will use it with the greatest\npleasure.\nI was so terribly disappointed that I\ndidn't see Harold and Bondie when they were\nhere. We talked over the telephone as perhaps\nHarold has told you as I was leaving that day\nfor a week's trip to southern Japan. We did\nhave a nice telephone visit however, and I\nheard all about the wonderful children and\ngrandchildren.\nLife goes on for us here in the same busy\nway and somehow, it is difficult to realize\nthat I will soon be here four years. That's\nquite a long time, isn't it?\nAs you know, we had a visit from \"Slim\"\nlast winter. I always enjoy seeing him and I\nthought this time he looked\nbetter than before.\nHis mother evidently is an invalid now from\nwhat I gathered.\nHaven't heard from Elma Stevenot in some\ntime but I believe that she has moved to San\nFrancisco. I was told that one daughter's\nmarriage had been very unhappy which I am\nsure must distress Elma terribly.",
      "-2-\nHow nice it would be to see you again\nand may be some day we can have that nice get-\ntogether and long talk.\nMuch love to you and yours and thanks again\nfor the lovely bag.\nMost fondly,",
      "19\nU\nAIR\n6 MAIL\nCENTS\nUNITED STATES OF AMERICA\nP\nMrs. Harold Bixby\n27 East 62nd Street\nNew York, New York\nLI3 LAIL Boll on\nLanding"
    ],
